1. DEFINITIONS

1.1. "Work" — the source code, tools, models, measurement datasets and
     documentation of this repository, and any derivatives thereof.

1.2. "Covered Product" — any product, service or internal process that
     (a) incorporates the Work or any part of it, or (b) was developed, tuned,
     accelerated or measured using the Work, or (c) contains results produced
     by the Work.

1.3. "Research Use" — use by a person or organisation that does NOT derive
     profit, directly or indirectly, from any Covered Product. Academic
     publication, teaching, reproduction of results and their open sharing are
     Research Use.

1.4. "Commercial Use" — any use not falling under 1.3, including internal use
     within an organisation that derives profit from a Covered Product,
     whether or not the Covered Product itself is distributed externally.

2. RESEARCH USE — FREE OF CHARGE

2.1. The copyright holder grants, free of charge, the right to use, reproduce,
     modify and distribute the Work for Research Use.

2.2. Conditions: retain this licence and attribution in all copies and
     derivatives; cite the source when publishing results.

2.3. Patent grant: to the extent necessary for Research Use, the copyright
     holder grants a non-exclusive, royalty-free licence to its patent rights.
     This grant terminates automatically if the recipient asserts patent claims
     against the Work.

3. COMMERCIAL USE — BY AGREEMENT

3.1. Commercial Use is NOT permitted under this licence.

3.2. Rights for Commercial Use are granted on contractual terms by agreement
     with the copyright holder: alex.xorm@gmail.com

3.3. Moving from Research Use to Commercial Use requires concluding an
     agreement BEFORE such use begins.

4. SCOPE

4.1. This licence covers the Work only. Third-party components placed in
     `vendor/` or otherwise marked retain their own licences; in case of
     conflict, the third-party licence prevails for that component.

4.2. Measurements and numerical results obtained on the user's own hardware
     belong to the user.

5. NO WARRANTY

THE WORK IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED,
INCLUDING WARRANTIES OF FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NON-INFRINGEMENT.
THE COPYRIGHT HOLDER SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY DAMAGES ARISING FROM USE OF
THE WORK.

In particular: the Work contains facilities that alter low-level behaviour of
compute kernels. Verifying the correctness of results on one's own hardware is
the user's responsibility.

6. TERMINATION

Rights under section 2 terminate automatically upon breach of this licence and
are reinstated once the breach is cured, unless the copyright holder states
otherwise.
